pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test (core membership, observed directly): under `strengthening_to_core on` the
% constraint a bare `red` introduces is a CORE constraint, so `deletion.rs` routes its deletion
% through checked deletion and refuses it without a justification -- the same refusal a formula
% constraint already got. While the `red` result was misclassified as derived this `del` was
% silently accepted, which is the cheapest direct observation of the misclassification.
f 1;
strengthening_to_core on;
red 1 y1 >= 1 : y1 -> 1 ;
del id 2 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
